WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.850
Each output is evidence for something
specific, against NIST's control catalog.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.168
The viewer role, and nothing that writes,

3
00:00:07.168 --> 00:00:10.188
supports monitoring an
external service provider.

4
00:00:10.188 --> 00:00:13.030
The run folder shows
every incident was read,

5
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:17.100
which also supports receiving
security alerts and advisories.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.375
A call nobody verified isn't run.

7
00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:22.936
And the gaps written down support
updating the risk assessment,

8
00:00:22.936 --> 00:00:27.237
which is the evidence this chapter adds
that no other provider chapter needs.

9
00:00:27.237 --> 00:00:28.941
The indicators are FedRAMP's,

10
00:00:28.941 --> 00:00:32.913
and which output supports which
indicator is the program's mapping.

11
00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:37.660
The kit's records support these controls;
the agency's assessor decides them.
